# Testing — head-toto

## Scope

The Makefile `test` target builds and runs **`build/tests/test_core`** (or
`build/tests/test_core.exe` on Windows).

Tests cover **NUM parsing** (`head_toto_parse_count()`), the **copy loops**
(`head_toto_copy_lines()`, `head_toto_copy_bytes()`) and the **elide loops**
(`head_toto_elide_lines()` / `_bytes()` and their `_stream()` variants) using
fixture files.
They do **not** exercise `main()`, the option parser, header output on real
stdout, or write-failure exits. There are **no** subprocess / integration
tests in-tree.

Tests run unchanged on Linux and Windows builds — there is no `SKIP` path.
Under **`HEAD_TOTO_WIN32_IO`**, fixtures are opened with `_O_BINARY`.

## Layout

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `tests/test_runner.c` | `main()` — invokes all suites in fixed order |
| `tests/test_count_parse.c` / `.h` | `head_toto_parse_count()` valid, suffixed, invalid, and overflow inputs |
| `tests/test_copy_lines.c` / `.h` | `head_toto_copy_lines()` with `\n` and `\0` delimiters |
| `tests/test_copy_bytes.c` / `.h` | `head_toto_copy_bytes()` short, exact, and over-length counts |
| `tests/test_elide_lines.c` / `.h` | `head_toto_elide_lines()` (seekable) and `_lines_stream()` give the same output |
| `tests/test_elide_bytes.c` / `.h` | `head_toto_elide_bytes()` (seekable) and `_bytes_stream()` give the same output |

Order in `test_runner.c`: count_parse → copy_lines → copy_bytes → elide_lines →
elide_bytes.

One scenario per `.c` / `.h` pair; headers declare `void test_<name>_run(void)`.

Test objects, the linked binary, and temporary fixtures live under
**`build/tests/`** (not under `tests/`).

## Framework

- No external framework — plain C with `<assert.h>`.
- Each case prints `PASS: <descriptive name>` on success.
- `assert()` failure → `abort()` → non-zero exit from `make test`.

## Build (from `Makefile`)

```makefile
TEST_CORE := $(TEST_BUILD_DIR)/test_core   # build/tests/test_core
LIB_OBJS  := $(BUILD_DIR)/head_toto_count.o \
             $(BUILD_DIR)/head_toto_io.o \
             $(BUILD_DIR)/head_toto_emit.o

$(TEST_CORE): $(TEST_OBJS) $(LIB_OBJS) $(HDRS) $(TEST_HDRS) | $(TEST_BUILD_DIR)
	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -o $@ $(TEST_OBJS) $(LIB_OBJS) $(LDFLAGS)

test: $(TEST_CORE)
	./$(TEST_CORE)
```

Tests link the library objects (`LIB_OBJS`) but **never `main.o`**, `head_toto_cli.o`,
or `head_toto_run.o`. They receive the same release `CFLAGS` as the main binary
(including `HEAD_TOTO_WIN32_IO` when applicable). `make test` must be run from
the repo root so fixture paths under `build/tests/` resolve.

## Fixtures

- Write input to `build/tests/fixture_<case>_in.tmp` with
  `open(O_WRONLY | O_CREAT | O_TRUNC | HEAD_TOTO_O_BINARY)`, close, reopen
  `O_RDONLY`.
- Copy into `build/tests/fixture_<case>_out.tmp`, close, read back into a stack
  buffer, compare with `memcmp()` and an exact length check.
- `remove()` both fixtures at the end of each case. `make clean` also deletes
  any leftovers under `build/tests/`.

## Required cases

1. **Count parsing:** `"0"` → 0, `"10"` → 10, `"007"` → 7, `" 5"` → 5,
   `"+5"` → 5, `"5K"` → 5120, `"K"` → 1024, `"1KB"` → 1000, `"1KiB"` → 1024,
   `"2b"` → 1024, `"1MB"` → 1000000;
   `""`, `" "`, `"-5"`, `"+K"`, `"5X"`, `"1Ki"`, `"1bB"`, `"5 "`, `"abc"` →
   `HEAD_TOTO_COUNT_INVALID` with `*out` untouched; a 40-digit string and
   `"20E"` → `HEAD_TOTO_COUNT_OVERFLOW`.
2. **Lines, fewer than N:** 3-line input, `n = 10` → output equals input.
3. **Lines, more than N:** 15-line input, `n = 10` → exactly the first 10 lines.
4. **Lines, no trailing newline:** `"a\nb"` with `n = 2` → `"a\nb"` (nothing appended).
5. **Lines, zero:** `n = 0` → empty output, return `0`.
6. **Lines, `\0` delimiter:** `"a\0b\0c\0"` with `n = 2`, `delim = '\0'` → `"a\0b\0"`.
7. **Lines, larger than buffer:** input with lines spanning `HEAD_TOTO_BUFSIZE`
   boundaries → correct prefix.
8. **Bytes:** `n` smaller than, equal to, and larger than input size; `n = 0` → empty.
9. **Bytes, CRLF:** `"a\r\nb\r\n"` with `n = 3` → `"a\r\n"` (verifies binary mode on Windows).
10. **Elide lines** (both variants, same expected output): `k = 0` → whole
    input; `k` larger than the line count → empty; `"x\ny\nz"` with `k = 1` →
    `"x\ny\n"`; `\0` delimiter; lines spanning `HEAD_TOTO_BUFSIZE` boundaries.
11. **Elide bytes** (both variants): `k = 0`, `k` below / equal to / above the
    input size; `"a\r\nb\r\n"` with `k = 2` → `"a\r\nb"`.
12. Never call `exit()` from a test; use `assert()` or `return` only.

## Adding tests

- Add `tests/test_<area>_<name>.c` + `.h`, declare runner in `.h`, call from
  `test_runner.c`, append to `TEST_SRCS` in `Makefile`.
- Use `HEAD_TOTO_O_BINARY` (from `head_toto_io.h`) for every fixture `open()`;
  no `#ifdef` branches that skip assertions.
- Keep tests allocation-free; stack buffers only (the code under test may
  allocate in the elide stream path).

## Manual smoke tests (not automated)

After `make`:

```sh
seq 20 > /tmp/n.txt
./build/head-toto /tmp/n.txt                 # expect: 1..10, exit 0
./build/head-toto -n 3 /tmp/n.txt            # expect: 1..3, exit 0
./build/head-toto -c 5 /tmp/n.txt            # expect: "1\n2\n3", exit 0
./build/head-toto /tmp/n.txt /tmp/n.txt      # expect: two ==> headers, blank line between
./build/head-toto -q /tmp/n.txt /tmp/n.txt   # expect: no headers
seq 5 | ./build/head-toto -n 2 -             # expect: 1, 2 from stdin
./build/head-toto missing /tmp/n.txt         # expect: error on stderr, then 1..10, exit 1
./build/head-toto -n abc /tmp/n.txt          # expect: invalid number of lines, exit 1
./build/head-toto --version                  # expect: head-toto <version>, exit 0
./build/head-toto --help                     # expect: usage text on stdout, exit 0
./build/head-toto -x                         # expect: invalid option + hint, exit 1
./build/head-toto -n -2 /tmp/n.txt           # expect: 1..18, exit 0
seq 20 | ./build/head-toto -c -3             # expect: 1..19 (drops "20\n"), exit 0
./build/head-toto -c 1K /tmp/n.txt           # expect: whole file (51 bytes), exit 0
./build/head-toto -5 /tmp/n.txt              # expect: 1..5, exit 0
./build/head-toto --v /tmp/n.txt             # expect: ambiguous option + hint, exit 1
{ ./build/head-toto -n 2; cat; } < /tmp/n.txt  # expect: 1..20 (offset left after line 2)
```

Compare against GNU `head` 9.4 with `diff <(head …) <(./build/head-toto …)` on
Linux (`LC_ALL=C`); stderr differs only in the program name.
